    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Camp-Pendleton-Campus-Center/Enrollment-Services-Director-I---CA_JR100606": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services Director I - CA",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nThe Enrollment Services Director I oversees enrollment, academic, and all other operational aspects of a specific campus location(s). This position serves as the University’s on-site representative responsible for identifying and engaging the installation in enrollment and community outreach initiatives. Position Accountabilities Responsible for the daily administrative operations of the site, including logistical aspects, record- keeping   and reporting. Maintain computer labs and classrooms. Ensure administrative records are properly scanned,   filed   and   submit   monthly reports as required .    Serve as the on-site resource for instructors concerning facility and equipment needs.         Serve as a key on-site connector for online and hybrid students affiliated with   their campus center ,   providing localized outreach, guidance, and relationship management throughout the enrollment lifecycle.   Meet monthly, quarterly, and annual   recruitment   goals   in order to   enroll students. Execute proactive and intentional notifications to students to complete necessary financial aid, registration and confirmation, active-duty   military   and Veteran’s benefits when applicable, and associated processes to ensure successful enrollment.  Collaborate with   Parkville   admissions, marketing, and enrollment teams to support the recruitment of online students by promoting Park University’s online programs to local military, corporate, and community partners tied to the region. Execute targeted outreach and follow-up strategies to cultivate online prospects, including virtual information sessions, one-to-one consultations, and coordinated communications aligned with Park’s broader enrollment strategy. Support the conversion of online inquiries and applicants by reinforcing program fit, degree pathways, military and employer benefits, and available student support services. Act as a steward for online students connected to the   Campus Center   by   facilitating   smooth handoffs between enrollment, academic advising, and student support functions to promote persistence and retention. Provide feedback to   University   leadership on regional demand, barriers, and opportunities related to online student recruitment and engagement to inform Park’s overall online enrollment strategy. C o lla b o rate   with   the Ed u cation   S e rvices   O fficer   ( ES O ) or   B u il d i n g L a nd l o r d   to en s u re a dh e r e n ce to installati o n   p o licies and   p r o ced u res .    B u il d   part n ers h i p s   with   l o cal   or g a n izati on s   t o   s u pport e n r o ll m e n t   g rowt h .   Assist   with   n e w s t ud e n t   recr u it m e n t efforts.   Co o r d i nate   with   University Relations and   Development   for site s p ecific   ad v e rtisi n g   and   d egree   p r o g ram   mar k eting   i n itiat iv es.   Responsible for the overarching A2E local strategy to foster quality enrollment growth by developing strategic pathways with partnering organizations . D e velop   b o t h   term   and   one - y ear   c o u rse   s ch ed u les   in conjunction with   Academic   Affairs .   Ma nag e   c l assr o o m   assig nm ents .    Work   closely with   t h e   Regional   Aca d e m ic Direct o r   w h er e   assig n e d . Meet term and year retention goals for your specific profile of students. Execute regularly scheduled check-ins for each student during progress to degree. Mitigate stop outs   relative   to Satisfactory Academic Progress, financial/personal distress, low attendance and/or academic performance, or general dissatisfaction by   utilizing   risk alerts and contacting students   in a timely manner . Work with students and   appropriate departments   to ensure   provision   of needed support services, such as Academic Support, Career Development, Campus Center Staff, Military and Veteran Student Services, and more. Provide basic information to students and connect students with these resource areas by setting appointments and conducting follow - up check-ins. Ensure students are aware of other services available, such as Counseling Center, Library, computer labs, Academic Advising and more.   Position Requirements: Bachelor’s   d e gr e e in   a p pr o p riate   field   required .     M ini m u m   2   y ears   of e x peri e n ce   preferred   i n op e rati o ns   an d   m anage m ent .    P r ef e r at least 1   y ear   of   t h at   e xp e ri e n ce   in h i gh e r   e ducati o n.   E x celle n t   o ral   a n d written   comm un icati o n   s k ills.   E x ce p ti on al cust o m er ser v ice   s k ills .    M u st   b e   a b le to work   with   a   d i v e rse   st ud e n t a n d fac u lty   p op u lati o n.   Strong   c o m pu ter s k ills,   proficie n cy   with   M S   Office pr o d u ct   s u ite.   A b ility   t o   qu ic k ly learn   n e w c o m pu ter s o f t ware   progr a m s .    S u fficient   k nowled g e   o f c o m pu ter   h ardwar e .   Detail   o rie n ted, or g a n ized   a n d a b ility to   m u l t i-tas k .   Physical Requirements     Must be able to navigate Campus Center locations which may require walking and climbing stairs.    Standing, lifting, carrying and basic   use   hand tools.   Visual acuity and ability to hear and communicate.    Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
