    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Assistant-Coach-Women-s-Volleyball-PT_JR100600": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach Women's Volleyball PT",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nPart time\n\nPosition Accountabilities Serve in a support role to the Head C oach   Assistance with all phases of the program (varsity and reserve) including coaching, recruiting, coordinating and organizing practices, scheduling, monitoring academics, weight room, player skill development, and skill evaluation   A ddi tional duties may include gameday administration, fundraising, game-related activities, and camps/ clinics.   Must have the ability to achieve certificatio n to transport students to team athletic events.   Other duties as assigned by the Head Coach & Director of Athletics.   Position Requirements: Bachelor’s degree preferred     College coaching and recruiting experience preferred.     Demonstrated successful experience in playing and/or coaching at collegiate, university, or professional level.   Knowledge of NAIA and Heart of America Athletic Conference rules and regulations.   A proven record of integrity, high principles and demonstrated ski ll in developing and motivating student athletes academically a nd athletically.   E xperience working with students from diverse backgrounds and cultures.   Valid Driver's license   Candidate must pass a pre- employment background investigation to be hired for this position.     Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Adjunct-Faculty---Interior-Design_JR100592": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Interior Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree or higher in Interior Design or a closely related design field, or a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the discipline or subfield relevant to the courses being taught. Candidates should also have a minimum of five years of professional experience in interior design or a closely related field, with demonstrated expertise relevant to the course(s) they will teach. Professional experience should be documented through a résumé and, when appropriate, a professional portfolio. Course Description AR282 Visual Communications I An introduction to basic drafting techniques, terminology, and symbols used in architectural drawings, using drafting equipment, lettering, plan and elevation construction with emphasis on proper line weight, quality, and scale; additionally study materials and fabrication techniques involved in the design and construction of interior details. AR296 Textiles for Interior Design This course explores the nature of man-made and natural materials used to produce textiles for use within the interior design industry. Content includes discussion of fibers, yarns, fabrics, finishes, design methods, construction, and proper application of these materials from technical, environmental and aesthetic approaches. AR289 Fundamentals of Interior Design An exploration of residential space planning problems applying the design process and space planning techniques to projects that emphasizes research and application of global design and the study of different cultures. Includes an intermediate review of life safety codes and accessibility guidelines. AR290 Interior Design Materials and Resources A survey of the materials and finishes utilized in interior applications through lecture, demonstrations, and/or field trips. Various methods of specification and estimation are reviewed, with students researching and assessing performance criteria including environmental ethics and social responsibility. AR382 Drawing Systems I An introduction to the principles and operations of computer generated drawing with an emphasis on producing both 2D (floor plans, elevations, etc.) and 3D (orthographic) drawings using AutoCAD."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Assistant-Professor-Business-Analytics_JR100591": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Business Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nPark University invites applications for a Full-Time tenure track Assistant Professor position starting in August 1, 2027 The successful candidate will primarily teach in-person, on-campus courses within Park University's Information Systems and Business Analytics programs. Our dynamic business analytics curriculum includes coursework in information systems, data mining, data visualization, predictive analytics, and digital marketing analytics. Students engage in hands-on, applied learning experiences that incorporate statistical analysis, programming, and data visualization tools to solve real-world business challenges. Position Accountabilities Teaching responsibilities will be aligned with the candidate’s academic background and professional expertise. In addition to face-to-face instruction, the teaching load may include online courses. Opportunities to develop and enhance online course offerings may also be available. The standard teaching assignment is four courses per semester. Position Requirements: Qualifications: Ph.D. or D.B.A (ABD or master’s degree considered) in business with a focus on Business Analytics including Information Systems, Data Analytics, or Data Science or a closely related field from a regionally accredited university.  Master’s degree with industry experience may be considered Proficiency in Python, R, SQL, and statistical software. Demonstrated teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level. Preferred Qualifications: Academic and/ or industry experience in: database systems data collection from multiple sources, including APIs. Business Analytics Experience teaching online courses Expertise in DevOps, data pipeline design, and cloud computing platforms, such as AWS. Qualified applicants must upload their curriculum vitae, cover letter, teaching philosophy, and professional references.  The cover letter must identify the candidate’s salary expectations. Review of applications begins October 19. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Director-Library-Services_JR100581-1": {
      "title": "Director Library Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nThe Director of Library Services provides strategic leadership for all functions of the library, collaborating with faculty and staff across the University to support Park’s mission and student learning outcomes. The Director is responsible for oversight of the Norrington Center, the physical location of the Library on the Parkville flagship campus, as well as the digital resources that serve Park students studying on campuses in six states and online. Position Accountabilities Responsible for defining and articulating the vision, strategic directions, and priorities for the future of the Library and for developing a dynamic environment that values creativity, teamwork, and innovation Oversees the development, delivery, and assessment of library services, resources, and programming in support of student learning. The position requires a commitment to student success and to the provision of excellent service, as well as strengths in outreach, collaboration, supervision, and assessment. Embraces emerging technologies; provides a combination of vision and practical management in response to the emergence of face-to-face, online, and hybrid educational experiences. Advocates on behalf of the Library both inside and outside the university and represents the library at local, state, regional, and national consortia and associations Works closely with administration and faculty to ensure that library resources, services, and programming meet the needs of the entire university community; measures service quality and makes improvements as needed. Serves as the facility supervisor for the Norrington Center, Campanella Gallery manager, and other campus units to ensure a safe and supportive learning environment for students Oversees the Fishburn Archives and processes for records retention and collections management, in collaboration with appropriate administrative offices Serves as project manager for library technology projects, and serves as the main point of contact with vendors Position Requirements: Master’s Degree in Library Science from an ALA-accredited institution. Education or experience in archives management and/or a second master’s or a doctoral degree is preferred but not required. Familiarity with trends and best practices in higher education and academic libraries A track record of progressively more responsible administrative, management, or leadership experience, preferably in an academic library with an emphasis on strategic planning, budget management, staff development, and emerging technologies Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to the core tenets of academic librarianship as articulated by the American Library Association’s Bill of Rights, Intellectual Freedom Principles for Academic Librarians, and Code of Ethics, as well as the Association of College and Research Libraries’ Framework for Information Literacy Strong interpersonal, communication, leadership, and collaboration skills, especially as they apply to the work of building and maintaining a respectful, collegial, and inclusive work environment Proven track record of successfully working with faculty, other department heads, and administrators to develop and deliver services that support teaching, learning, and scholarship Demonstrated leadership and communication techniques that exemplify transparency and accountability, that build trust between and among individuals and groups, and that elicit creativity, commitment, and high performance from employees Proven successes in the development, delivery, and assessment of library collections and services Preferred Qualifications: Experience with program evaluation, assessment, and accreditation practices Demonstrated knowledge of information technology as it relates to libraries, and the ability to effectively communicate with technologists, administration, and library personnel about technology Experience with the development and delivery of library services to distance and online students Ability to perform administrative functions for a range of online information tools and databases Experience developing and implementing user-centered digital projects Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-Campus/Scholarship-Coordinator_JR100584": {
      "title": "Scholarship Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nThe purpose of this position is to ensure the effective, accurate, and student-centered administration of the University's scholarship programs while providing exceptional service to students and campus stakeholders. The Scholarship Coordinator works collaboratively with university departments to promote consistent scholarship processes, maintain the integrity of scholarship programs, and support institutional efforts to enhance student access, affordability, and success. Position Accountabilities •    Coordinate the day-to-day administration of institutional scholarship programs. •    Assist with the scholarship application, review, awarding, renewal, and disbursement processes. •    Ensure scholarship awards are processed accurately, timely, and in accordance with University policies and established procedures. •    Maintain accurate scholarship records within the student information system and other applicable software. •    Review scholarship applications and verify eligibility based on established criteria. •    Prepare scholarship materials and provide administrative support for scholarship committees. •    Review scholarship renewal eligibility, including GPA, enrollment status, and other established requirements. •    Process scholarship revisions resulting from enrollment changes or other eligibility updates. •    Assist the Advancement Office with the administration of privately funded scholarship programs. •    Help ensure donor restrictions and scholarship criteria are accurately applied. •    Collect and maintain scholarship recipient information to support donor stewardship activities. •    Provide administrative support for the athletic scholarship awarding process in collaboration with Athletics and Financial Aid. •    Compile routine reports related to scholarship awards, utilization, and recipient data. •    Maintain accurate records to support reporting, audits, and compliance requirements. •    Assist in documenting and maintaining scholarship policies, procedures, and operational guidelines. •    Provide scholarship information and customer service to prospective and current students, families, faculty, and staff. •    Develop and maintain effective working relationships with Admissions, Advancement, Academic Affairs, Athletics, Financial Aid, and other campus partners. •    Coordinate with academic departments regarding department-specific scholarship processes. •    Participate on scholarship committees and other meetings as assigned.   Position Requirements: • Bachelor’s Degree required. •    Preference given to candidates with experience in financial aid, scholarships, admissions, or enrollment management. •    Experience working with student information systems, scholarship management software, or relational databases preferred.   •    Demonstrated commitment to providing exceptional customer service and fostering positive relationships with students, families, faculty, and staff. •    Excellent organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. •    Strong attention to detail and a high level of accuracy in processing records and maintaining confidential information. •    Ability to analyze information, solve problems, and exercise sound judgment in interpreting policies and procedures. •    Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. •    Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to interact effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. •    Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. •    Ability to learn new technologies and adapt to changing processes and priorities. •    Commitment to providing equitable, student-centered service while supporting the University's mission and values. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Return-of-Title-IV-Specialist_JR100536": {
      "title": "Return of Title IV Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-10\nFull time\n\nThe Return to Title IV Specialist is a role within our Financial Aid division of Student Financial Services. This role is responsible for understanding and maintaining compliance within the function of Return of Title IV. This position is responsible for reviewing and understanding Federal Methodology as it pertains to R2T4, leading the R2T4 team within SFA in the areas of Return of Title IV adjustments, Reaffirmations, lender notifications, and “WF” grade report. Will have full working knowledge of all aspects of the drop and withdraw process; Will have full working knowledge of the complexities of R2T4 decision making in a module-heavy environment; Oversees completion of daily workload and resolves student issues when they require special handling; Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, making professional judgement decisions on these appeals independently; Assists other staff in the absence of the Associate Director, ensures completion of scheduled tasks within assigned deadlines, and assists in achieving departmental and organizational goals. This position is data-heavy with a full working knowledge of excel required. Position Accountabilities Maintaining compliance within the Return of Title IV (R2T4) function in a module based environment Leading the Return of Title IV team to ensure that goals and deadlines are met within the allowed error rate of less than 5% Processing the Return of Title IV calculations and aid adjustments Ensuring the integrity of the add/drop data and integration of that data into PowerFaids Processing of “WF” report at end of each session to process R2T4 on students who fail due to not completing the term Managing the reaffirmation process for students returning to attendance within a semester Ensure adjustments and returns are completed in a timely manner compliant with federal regulations Maintain professional working relationship with Registrar and Student Account departments Manages the Satisfactory Academic Progress Appeal process from start to finish, performing professional judgement decisions independently, working with students, Academic Success Center, and academic advisors to ensure student success following an appeal Assists Student Financial Aid Operations team in the absence of the Associate Director; this requires full knowledge of Title IV regulations and how they impact all functional areas of the financial aid office Other duties as assigned Position Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree required as position is compliance based. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired. Ability to work within complex data systems (CX/Jenzabar, PowerFaids). Expected to have a thorough ability to use Excel to manage data (ability to manipulate and interpret data using v-lookup, pivot tables, etc.). Leadership characteristics are required with the ability to hold self and coworkers to high standards in accuracy, deadlines, output, and compliance. Ability to train coworkers in Return to Title IV and other areas of expertise Ability to resolve problems and communicate professionally orally and in writing. Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to maintain good working relationships with outside departments. Ideal candidate would be committed to learning all aspects of the operations of Park Student Financial Aid. Strong orientation toward a high volume and fast-paced environment with demonstrated experience in compliance. Must be able to maintain exceptional level of accuracy while meeting tight deadlines. Previous experience in financial aid or equivalent combination of education and experience is required. Previous experience in Return to Title IV is desired Ability to work independently and make professional judgement decisions on SAP Appeals Ability to multitask, organize and establish priorities are required. Founded in 1875, Park University is a private, liberal arts university. Park’s flagship campus is located in the Kansas City suburb of Parkville, Missouri, on the bluffs overlooking the Missouri River.  We offer an excellent benefits package including health, dental, and life insurance, retirement plan, and tuition-paid undergraduate classes for employees and dependents. Park University is an equal-opportunity employer and encourages applications from women and minorities. Qualified applicants must upload a resume and cover letter that includes salary requirements."
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Parkville-MO/Adjunct-Instructor---Nursing-Clinical-Adjunct_JR100018": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Nursing Clinical Adjunct",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-08\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is a face to face course. Local applicants only.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. The Ellen Finley Earhart Department of Nursing at Park University invites applicants to apply for a Clinical Adjunct Faculty position. The clinical adjunct faculty is a valued member of our Nursing Program team. They are responsible for facilitating student learning in a variety of clinical care areas, grading of student learning assessments, collaborating with department faculty, and working with nursing unit staff and patients to assure the safety and quality of our program clinical course work. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s of Science in Nursing (BSN) 3 years of RN experience in the last 5 years Completion of the MHA clinical adjunct academy Unencumbered RN License in Missouri or a multistate license Current American Heart Association BLS certification for the Health Care Provider Positive Employer Evaluations Course Description Our clinical rotations vary depending on clinical placement availability with our clinical partners, as well as the clinical day hours vary by course. Our clinical partners are located throughout the Greater Kansas City area and St. Joseph, MO. North Kansas City Hospital NUR320 Fundamentals Clinicals Saturday Sessions NUR335 Adult Heath I NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)  St Luke’s East NUR335 Adult Heath I St Luke’s North NUR335 Adult Heath I Signature Psychiatric Hospital at North Kansas City NUR356 Mental Health  ​Signature Psychiatric Hospital at Liberty ​NUR356 Mental Health University of Kansas NUR435 Adult Health II (critical care)"
    },
    "https://park.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/ParkUniversityCareers/job/Cheyenne-WY/Adjunct-Instructor----Mathematics-MA102--MA120--MA125_JR100003": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor -- Mathematics MA102, MA120, MA125",
      "description": "Posted: 2024-12-18\nPart time\n\nAppointments are made on a term-by-term basis. Adjunct faculty are required to successfully complete an online Canvas LMS orientation course before being scheduled, as well as other training if required by the department. This is an on-site blended/hybrid course, students attend class in person 60% of the time and complete the remaining 40% online through Park’s Canvas Learning Management System.   Local applicants only please.   A background check and government security clearance will be required to get on base.   Click on Park University Locations for more information on our campus centers. Click on Park University’s Catalog for more information on programs and courses. To ensure timely submission of your credentials, qualified applicants should apply following the specific instructions noted in each job posting. For all positions, a Masters Degree in the relevant field is required, along with related work and/or academic experience. For most postings, a Ph.D. or other terminal degree is preferred. Park University is an Equal Opportunity Employer encouraging applications from women and minorities. The university will recruit and employ qualified personnel and will provide equal opportunities during employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability or status as a qualified protected veteran. Click   here   to view Park University’s EEOC and related policies. Please Note: Park University participates in E-Verify for all positions at all campus center locations nationwide. Minimum Qualifications MA102 Introductory Algebra Master’s Degree in Mathematics related field. MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics Masters in Mathematics or a Masters in Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Masters in Statistics, Actuarial Science, Finance, or Economics will also be considered. MA125 Intermediate Algebra Masters in Mathematics or Applied Mathematics. Candidates with a Master’s degree in Statistics, Physics, Mathematical Education, Operations Research, Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Finance, Actuarial Science or Economics will also be considered. Course Description MA102 Introductory Algebra This developmental course prepares students to complete Parks Liberal Education mathematics requirement. Topics include integer arithmetic, basic algebraic equations, rational numbers, percentages, and basic graphing.  MA120 Basic Concepts of Statistics A development of certain basic concepts in probability and statistics that are pertinent to most disciplines. Topics include: probability models, discrete random variables, normal distributions, confidence intervals, and hypothesis testing. MA125 Intermediate Algebra This course provides a transition into college level Mathematics courses. Topics include the real number system, basic operations of algebra, linear, quadratic and rational equations, inequalities, radicals and exponents, and systems of equations."
    }
  },
